# Configuration for the Facebook Marketplace extractor.
# `just setup` generates .env for you; this file documents every option.
#
# The scraper needs an authenticated Facebook session. Two ways to provide it:

# --- Option A (recommended): reuse a logged-in Chrome profile ----------------
# Point at a user-data dir that contains a profile signed into facebook.com.
# The scraper launches Chrome with channel=chrome against this directory.
# On Linux/macOS the OS keychain decrypts the cookies, so the profile must be
# copied (not moved) from the same machine/user. `just setup` copies it to
# ~/.local/share/fme-chrome and writes these three lines for you.
#
#   FME_USER_DATA_DIR=/home/you/.local/share/fme-chrome
#   FME_BROWSER_CHANNEL=chrome
#   FME_PROFILE_DIRECTORY=Default

# --- Option B: email/password login ------------------------------------------
# Used only when FME_USER_DATA_DIR is empty. A captcha/security check must be
# solved manually in the browser window on every new session, so this is mostly
# a fallback for machines without a logged-in Chrome profile.
#
#   FME_USERNAME=you@example.com
#   FME_PASSWORD=super-secret

# --- Optional: `just sync` remote -------------------------------------------
# Where `just sync` sends (or pulls) the data/ directory. Both are optional; the
# defaults point at the project's usual server. A relative dir resolves against
# the remote user's $HOME. Override per-run with `just sync --host/--dir`.
#
#   FME_SYNC_REMOTE=maxi@192.168.0.235
#   FME_SYNC_REMOTE_DIR=Projects/romayengineer/fme

# --- Optional: PocketBase data directory -------------------------------------
# Where `just save`/`just serve` keep the SQLite database. Defaults to ./pb_data
# in the project root (so it stays under .gitignore); set this to relocate it.
#
#   FME_PB_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/fme/pb_data

# --- Optional: heat map basemaps ---------------------------------------------
# `just heatmap -map=<id>` selects the basemap (see `just heatmap-maps`). The only
# built-in map is `leaflet-esri` (Esri World Street Map), which works without an
# API key; the CARTO and OpenStreetMap basemaps were removed because they require
# an API key (see docs/heatmap_basemaps.md). To add a future provider that needs a
# key, pass it with -map-token, or set the provider's env var here (e.g.
# FME_MAPBOX_TOKEN); never commit real tokens.
#
#   FME_MAPBOX_TOKEN=
#   FME_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY=
